Authentication and databases sit underneath almost every app you'll build, yet they are often the parts developers understand least. You copy a login flow from a tutorial, or a query works and you're not quite sure why. Things hold up until a session expires unexpectedly or a query slows down, and then you have to work out what's going on.

Today, we're launching two new YouTube channels to help with that: **Learn Auth** and **Learn Postgres**.

Both channels follow the same format. Each episode takes one topic and explains it in about two minutes, built around a single picture that stays on screen the whole time. Every episode ends with a quick quiz, and each one comes with an under-a-minute Short when you only want the core idea.

# Meet Learn Auth

[Learn Auth](https://www.youtube.com/@LearnAuth) explains how sign-in really works. Your app has a bouncer and a guest list, your session is a wristband, and your JWT is a signed hall pass. Each metaphor gives you something concrete to remember after the video ends.

The channel is made for developers adding sign-in to their first app, students, and frontend and mobile developers who want auth to make sense. No prior auth knowledge is needed.

**Season 1 covers how login works:**

- Authentication vs authorization
- Password hashing
- Sessions and cookies
- JWT
- OAuth 2
- 2FA codes
- Passkeys
- Magic links and email codes
- Password reset

The first episodes are already live, starting with the difference between who you are and what you're allowed to do:

{% youtube id="wN5Wr2iZZUw" title="Authentication vs authorization: the bouncer and the guest list" /%}

[**Subscribe to Learn Auth on YouTube**](https://www.youtube.com/@LearnAuth)

# Meet Learn Postgres

[Learn Postgres](https://www.youtube.com/@LearnPostgres) teaches the SQL every developer needs, using the same one-picture approach. Your tables have a group chat, your query takes the stairs, and your table has a bouncer.

It's made for developers meeting their first relational database, students, and frontend and mobile developers who want their queries to make sense. All you need to know is SELECT.

**Season 1 covers SQL fundamentals:**

- Joins
- Indexes
- EXPLAIN ANALYZE
- NULL
- Transactions and ACID
- Primary and foreign keys
- Data types
- Constraints
- Upsert

Episodes on joins, indexes, EXPLAIN ANALYZE, NULL, transactions, and primary and foreign keys are already published. The channel also covers Postgres news, starting with a breakdown of November's minor releases and the 52 CVEs they fix. Start with the episode on joins:

{% youtube id="V7BYYkmj2lc" title="SQL joins explained: your tables have a group chat" /%}

[**Subscribe to Learn Postgres on YouTube**](https://www.youtube.com/@LearnPostgres)

# Stay connected

Both channels also post on X and Instagram, so you can follow along for new episodes and quick lessons wherever you spend your time:

- **Learn Auth:** [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/@LearnAuth) · [X](https://x.com/learnauth) · [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/learnauth/)
- **Learn Postgres:** [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/@LearnPostgres) · [X](https://x.com/learnpostgres) · [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/learnpostgres/)

# Start watching

New episodes are rolling out through Season 1, so now is a good time to subscribe and learn alongside them. Two minutes is enough to finally understand the thing you've been copying from tutorials.

When you're ready to put it into practice, [Appwrite Auth](/products/auth) handles sign-up, sign-in, sessions, OAuth, 2FA, passkeys, and permissions for you, and you can run the queries yourself on [Appwrite's managed Postgres](https://appwrite.io/products/postgres), with an SQL editor right in the Console.

See you in the comments.
